{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The fear of YHWH is the beginning of wisdom</b> — like the sense of: <i>The fear of YHWH is the beginning of wisdom</i> [Proverbs 1:7]." "<b>And the knowledge of holy ones is understanding</b> — its meaning is: the beginning of understanding is the knowledge of holy ones." "<b>And the knowledge of holy ones</b> — they interpreted it concerning the blessed Name, as it says: <i>for Elohim is holy</i> [1 Samuel 2:2]. And the meaning is: for the beginning of the generation of understanding is the existence of the Name. And it is possible to interpret: the knowledge of holy ones is the apprehension of the existence of the separate intelligences and all the spiritual beings, for knowledge of their existence is the core of understanding, and from it one ascends to the existence of the highest degree, and just as if there is no fear there is no wisdom, so if there is no knowledge there is no understanding."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:43.774102324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}